Author: Alex Lindsay <alexander.lindsay@inl.gov>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 16:52:20 2026 -0700

    Exclude VI active-set residuals from reference residual norms

    PETSc 3.26 keeps a user convergence test when the SNES type is set to
    vinewtonrsls, so MOOSE's Convergence objects now decide convergence of
    variational inequality solves. Previously PETSc replaced the test with
    SNESConvergedDefault_VI, which measures the residual only over the
    inactive set.

    At degrees of freedom held at a bound the residual is not driven to zero,
    since the bound constraint holds there in place of the residual equation.
    ReferenceResidualConvergence included those entries in its per-variable
    residual norms, so the relative check stalled on a converged solve and
    the step was cut back to dtmin (e.g. TMAP8 val-2d). Zero the active-set
    entries, as reported by SNESVIGetActiveSetIS, before computing the norms.

    refs idaholab#33833

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

